From d34e7aff62e238bafebfb7d4909c5f1012ff30b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 08:15:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Invalidate model.options memo when asynchronous
 pricing changes

The post-#3411 controlled hub A/B reached 2.71 ms warm median but only 84/100
byte-equal pairs: Nous pricing/pricing_pending changed after pricing warmers
published, while the payload memo had no pricing stamp. Fixture visibility and
credential-key mutation checks alone did not exercise this input.

Stamp pricing publication generation, provider endpoint-cache selection,
expired pricing deadlines and cached Nous entitlement. Preserve normal pricing
cleanup and keep the existing memo TTL and read-only worker controls unchanged.

Proof: five behavioral RED cases on main (publication/replacement/expiry/
endpoint mapping/entitlement); GREEN after fix. Thirty pricing consumer files:
792 passed, one skipped. Five pricing-stamp mutants killed by real payload
parity assertions. Original 13-test J visibility suite also passes. Full
scripts/check: 20 checks green. Hub acceptance must be rerun after deployment.
